<id/03/0355/#concept> a <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E55_Type>, skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Gambier"@en ;
    skos:broadMatch <customs-1866/plant/#concept> ;
    skos:broader <id/grp/grp_vegetable_tannins/#concept> ;
    skos:definition "an extract prepared at Singapore from the *Uncaria Gambir*, and used as a dye and tanning substance. It is misnamed in trade circles *Terra Japonica*. The imports in the last few years have averaged 6000 tons per annum. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 180]"@en ;
    skos:editorialNote "Curated classification (wd_term=gambier; wd_relation=skos:exactMatch): Gambier (Uncaria gambir extract) has its own Wikidata item; it had been close-matched to catechu (Acacia cutch). Layer-1 observations: 108 rows, 1861–1920. Series: HCPP_Annual Statement of Trade ×108. Units: Tons ×84; CWTS (Hundredweights) ×24. Top routes: World → United Kingdom ×29; Straits Settlements → United Kingdom ×14; Singapore and Eastern Straits Settlements → United Kingdom ×13; Other Foreign Countries → United Kingdom ×8."@en ;
    skos:exactMatch <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q19840126> ;
    skos:inScheme <id/scheme/#resource> ;
    skos:notation "0355" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Gambier"@en ;
    skos:related <id/02/0206/#concept> ;
    skos:scopeNote "Historical Southeast Asian vegetable tanning extract (Uncaria gambir); closely allied in 19th-century British trade ledgers with Cutch and Terra Japonica."@en ;
